        <inbodydescription>
<para>projection of a gravity vector (e.g. (0,-1,0) ) onto a vector r(r[0],r[1],r[2]) r is a vector from one node to the other of the line element. (where |r|=1) We then perform the projection of the gravity vector on the line element</para>
<para>projection of vector g(0,-1, 0) onto a surface with a normal vector n(n[0], n[1], n[2]) (where |n|=1) is equal to n x (n x g) = (n, g) n - g = -n[1] n - g This code obviously assumes all nodes of the element are co-planar</para>
        </inbodydescription>
